WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:58.420
The soul that used to be in this body
will never be at peace.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:06.090
Further out is a planet
where intelligent life forms live...

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.500
...and here, people took the act
of giving birth and raising children...

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.770
...far too much for granted.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:23.320
Reunion

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.260
<i>We don't know when the enemy</i>
<i>will attack next!</i>

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.620
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:40.220
<i>I don't want to hear anything as stupid as</i>
<i>not being able to use the newly-built ship!</i>

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.810
Amuro, how are you?

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.910
Even these robots know about stuff
that happened long ago...

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.250
...yet I forget stuff
that just happened recently.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.520
They're beginning the construction
of the Gundam Mk. II's flying armor.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.930
I know!

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.100
Why not try to get used to the military?

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.140
At this rate, you'll continue being
"corrected" by Mr. Wong.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.300
Corrected?

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.310
It's a military term for hitting someone
to wake him up.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:21.070
The Argama crew have been soft on you
because they aren't regular forces.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:21.970
I'll be careful.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.510
- Hi! You're here!
- Sorry we're late!

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.170
We're bringing in the materials.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.680
The flying armor?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.480
Yeah.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.950
Remember you talked to me
about the "Zeta Gundam" thing?

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.950
Yes. For entry into the atmosphere.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.080
We've completed a prototype, and
will send the Mk. II into the atmosphere...

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.020
...using its transforming parts.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.060
When are we entering the atmosphere?!

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:44.160
Today, we'll be headed in that direction
after leaving here.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.830
- Where to?
- Where else, but Jaburo?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.870
To the Earth Federation Forces' base?

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.130
- Now it's used as the Titans' rear base.
- But...!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.470
This has features other than the wave rider,
doesn't it?

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.140
Yes, it can also be operated as a hovercraft
for battle on Earth.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.550
That's why we captured
the Titans' battleship at Granada.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.670
Will there be a fleet
coming from Granada as well?

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.280
Yes. Six vessels from Granada.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.410
From here, there will be the Argama
and two other vessels.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:09.620
That many?

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.180
We'll have about eighty mobile suits.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:20.300
But won't staging an attack on Earth
mean we'll pollute it?

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.270
We won't use any nuclear
or chemical weapons...

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.600
...and if we can crush the Titans' base,
that'll mark an end to this whole conflict.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.470
Do you think so?

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.640
Wouldn't crushing Gryps be a better idea?

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.740
No.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:38.080
Lieutenant Quattro, you're not really
in favor of this operation, are you?

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.320
Well...

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:43.320
...there is a possibility that the Republic of
Zeon may join forces with the Titans.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.290
We must stamp out the source of the fire!

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.510
The Marasai could have been used
by the A.E.U.G. to test their mobile suits.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.480
And Anaheim will supply the A.E.U.G.
with high performance mobile suits?

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.910
That way they'd have a valid excuse
whichever side wins the war.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.680
The only quality a soldier really needs
is to be able to shout loudly.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:20.990
- Have we arrived?!
- Yes, we're opening the front hatch, sir!

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:30.160
Jamaican's given you permission to take off
provided you test the Marasai as well.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.670
- Me?
- Yeah.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.830
So, won't you take part in my plan?

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.530
We'll attack together
but make it look like one unit.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:39.080
A delayed attack.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:43.310
I guess I couldn't face Lila if I were
removed as a Titans pilot, after all.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:47.050
Yes, the Sichuan left
after getting special orders from Gryps.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:49.180
They left the port without
filing a destination report with us.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.990
We need to record the information
for our monthly reports.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.930
Please tell us where it is headed.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.790
It's a military secret!

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.770
Our organization is also an arm
of the regular forces.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.500
It's the unit confidentiality! Dismissed!

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:02.900
Yes, sir!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.310
Well?

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.870
It is the Sichuan, but it's been painted
a different color.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.840
I can't tell.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.650
As a sailor, I can tell
the subtle differences.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.180
I see, then let's leave here at once.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:19.380
Yes, sir!

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.950
What about the plans Kacricon
came up with?

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.820
That'll be an appropriate gift
when we leave the Moon.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:25.860
Yes, sir!

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.860
Prepare to depart!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.440
Mad Hatter here.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.380
<i>Alice wants to get rid of her hat.</i>

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:45.610
Confirming Mad Hatter!

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.110
The Argama's taking off.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.910
Good! Let's hit them hard!

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.260
- Got it?! It's a delayed attack plan!
- <i>Yeah, I know!</i>

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:06.900
Great acceleration!

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:15.670
Though it may be a windfall,
I shouldn't underestimate this chance.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:27.420
We'll destroy the Gundam Mk. II
no matter what!

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:42.800
We're departing!

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.900
- Detecting incoming missiles!
- What?!

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.150
Enemy attack?! From where?!

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.080
Not bad. The Argama
can no longer depart.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.790
Alice, can you hear me?! Adjust angle!

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:03.950
To your left, 0.01 degrees!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.350
Please send out the mobile suits, sir!

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.230
You're in no position to give me orders!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.350
I'm doing it!

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:14.760
Damn!

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.460
- <i>Don't forget to guard the front!</i>
- R-Roger!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.170
You're taking too long!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.300
We were still making adjustments
for this thing!

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.350
For the flying armor?

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.750
Kamille! Mk. II, launching!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.310
<i>Thanks!</i>

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:36.160
So those are the Nemos.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.270
How about this?!

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:15.990
It's Kamille!

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.200
There's an enemy!

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:33.640
<i>Take a weapon! Use the anti-air artillery!</i>

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.040
<i>Can't you get it attached yet?!</i>

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.450
<i>We'll be done once the circuits</i>
<i>are manually connected.</i>

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.040
<i>Hurry! What about the anti-air artillery?!</i>

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.510
Kacricon!

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.180
I see the Gundam Mk. II!

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:47.560
<i>Ignore the other mobile suits!</i>
<i>We'll lure him away from the others!</i>

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.090
I may not even have to trouble
Jerid with this.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:53.930
A mobile suit just came in?!

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.500
A-A new model?!

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.370
There he goes, Jerid!

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.270
Got it, Kacricon!

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.380
The data bank has this model on record.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:14.920
A Marasai?

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.860
Showing his back to an enemy?!

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.460
How'd he turn so fast?!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.110
It must be a new model.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.480
Two units?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:49.310
Above me! No, that's what the enemy
wants me to do!

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:01.130
That's such an outdated maneuver.
You're there!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.840
What a guy!

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:15.350
Is this also that Kamille guy?!

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.980
Just watch me, petite-mobiles!

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.490
Not bad for some petite-mobiles!

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:35.960
<i>Lieutenant Emma, protect the fleet!</i>
<i>I'll go get Kamille!</i>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.160
Roger!

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.150
Thanks to enemy mobile suits
being so close...

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.150
...the enemy spaceships won't dare fire
any missiles.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.440
Don't panic.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:50.710
With the Minovsky particles
so densely scattered...

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:51.810
...I can't get in touch
with Kamille's mobile suit.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.620
There are times we can detect him by chance!
Keep trying!

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:55.660
Yes, sir!

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:59.020
Anti-air artillery! Don't fire at
any of our mobile suits!

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.810
- Say your prayers!
- What?!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.090
Too bad you won't live long enough
to be a great pilot!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.890
Energy of this amount must be from the...!

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:40.060
I still don't have enough energy
to fire again!

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.800
Not by mere flea-like mobile suits!

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:48.910
The gold guy!

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.400
Jerid!

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.410
Our plan's failed, we'll fight separately!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.490
- You're not getting away!
- <i>Kamille!</i>

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:11.860
<i>You've drifted too far from the battle lines.</i>
<i>The Argama's departed!</i>

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.200
How's Amman?

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.860
You guys carry out the plan!

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:19.700
We're able to use our mining machinery
as weapons if we need to!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:20.600
Mr. Wong.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:23.240
Kamille! We're heading back to the Argama!

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:25.840
Yes! But, here they come again!

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:26.880
What?!

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:30.040
Ignore them!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.050
- But...!
- Come!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.120
Are we just going to let them get away?!

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.230
We lost our chance!

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:49.770
We'll head back to the Alexandria!

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:56.100
<i>Fire missiles at once. We'll recover our</i>
<i>mobile suits while they're being shot!</i>

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:58.610
<i>Vessels detected leaving Granada!</i>

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:00.740
<i>This is the image we got</i>
<i>from the special camera.</i>

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:02.370
Those A.E.U.G....!

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.680
Where are they planning to go?

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:15.050
Didn't the guys from Granada destroy
the Alexandria and Bosnia?!

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.120
No, sir! I haven't confirmed
any destroyed ships!

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.170
That's expecting a little too much, Captain!

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:25.240
We cannot expect that much from a fleet
overloaded with mobile suits.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:28.000
I'm talking more from the viewpoint
of morale!

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.110
We can't invade Jaburo if we're supported
by the people from Granada!

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:34.080
If we go ahead and do it,
I don't see why not.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:35.710
We'll wait thirty minutes!

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.310
If we're certain they're
no longer pursuing us...

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.350
...we'll head for our rendezvous point!

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.830
We're finally going to attack Jaburo.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:50.590
This is really something.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.060
<i>Kamille Bidan!</i>

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:56.190
Yes?

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:57.260
<i>There you are.</i>

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.740
<i>You fought well</i>
<i>during the Amman battle.</i>

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:03.710
<i>Without your defense, we would still</i>
<i>be stuck in that basement port.</i>

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:07.710
<i>As captain, and on behalf of the entire crew,</i>
<i>I express our gratitude for your help.</i>

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.610
Thank you very much.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:13.290
<i>Stay on duty for a little while longer,</i>
<i>and then go get some rest!</i>

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.350
Thank you very much!

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:18.190
You fought very well today.

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.230
Really?

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:21.390
Yo, Newtype.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.400
Please stop calling me that,
even if you're only joking.

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:26.120
Where are you going?

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.790
- I want to check on Haro.
- But you're still on duty!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.230
Let him go.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.330
I'll cover for Kamille until he gets back!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.400
Thank you very much!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.610
All available crew!
Scan the surrounding area!

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.490
- Looks like it <i>is</i> a ship.
- Does it?

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.360
Scanning for an enemy off the port side!

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:00.400
What?!

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.900
I've also detected a silhouette
of a mobile suit-like object!

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.940
Come on.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:10.640
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:16.080
Don't let Haro fly!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.520
Haro will avoid you!

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.350
Liar!

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.650
I want you on standby!

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.320
<i>Confirmed model of the damaged ship!</i>

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:29.520
<i>An atmospheric shuttle!</i>
<i>I believe it's the Temptation.</i>

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:32.120
The Temptation?!
That's Captain Bright's ship!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:33.260
Do you know him?

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.960
Commander Bright Noa,
the former captain of the White Base.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.930
The White Base?

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:39.900
Okay, come with me!

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:41.700
Kamille! Launching!

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.250
Quattro Bajeena! Hyaku Shiki!
Launching!

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.060
Lieutenant Quattro! I'm sending it out!

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.100
<i>Roger!</i>

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:10.000
Mega Bazooka Launcher, lift off!

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:30.960
I hope it works.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.030
Why is the shuttle flying in this area?

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:56.070
- Don't waste any shots!
- Yes, sir!

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.120
They might've not noticed us...

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:02.580
...and it's possible the fleet we transmitted
to for help may belong to the Titans.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:03.750
Captain!

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:06.690
I see the wake of a mobile suit-like object.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.460
Friend?! Or foe?!

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:09.660
Anyone pursuing?

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:12.030
It's become silent, but...!

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:43.690
What?!

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.700
What was that?!
It looked like a mobile armor.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:49.930
A mobile armor?

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.340
Is this pressure I'm feeling
from whoever's in that?

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:28.340
Kamille!

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:34.350
He attacked the Temptation!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.180
What a coward!

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:48.590
I missed him!

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.860
Kamille! Scatter the
extinguishing spray!

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:54.490
Roger!

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:06.280
Rescue's arrived!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:07.840
Please rest assured!

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:09.280
Please remain seated!

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.750
There's no worry of
the engine exploding!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.240
I heard from Lieutenant Quattro.
You say it was a mobile armor?

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:37.400
It's not in the data bank,
and I can't confirm it by sight.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:40.240
I couldn't even come close
to making contact.

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:42.310
- But...!
- Don't let it bother you.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:46.580
Considering the size of the Titans' Gryps,
it's not surprising what they come up with.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:47.710
You're right.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:51.360
Please look after this. I'll help reload
after I take a shower.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.090
- Get some sleep!
- Thank you.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.430
We'll be confirming everybody's identity...

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:03.440
...so first, please get a number
from the clerk in front of you...

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:06.170
...and begin by telling us which colony
you're from. From here you'll be taken...

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:11.140
I've once again taken the role of a captain
who loses his ship.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:14.770
There's no need to feel bad
about the White Base.

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:16.410
To the Earth Federation Forces...!

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:20.810
No, that still makes no difference to the
fact that it was destroyed, Captain Quattro.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.750
I'm a Lieutenant, Commander Bright.

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:29.730
Let me introduce you to Kamille Bidan.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.820
He pilots the Gundam Mk. II.

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:33.760
Kamille?

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:36.670
You gave me your autograph once,
back at Green Oasis.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.170
Th-Thank you for saving us.

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:42.300
Kamille!

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:45.170
- Kamille...!
- Fa! Fa Yuiry!

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.810
I didn't think I'd ever see you again!

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:50.210
Kamille!

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:52.710
Fa...!

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:03.030
Fa. What's wrong?

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:06.620
Both dad and mom have been captured
by Bask of the Titans!

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:09.330
By Bask? But why?!

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:13.200
Because they know you, Kamille,
since you stole the Gundam Mk. II.

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:14.870
That's why...!

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:17.210
Bask would...!

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:19.640
Bask Om would do something like that.

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:24.880
And you, Fa?

00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:28.290
Captain Bright saved me.

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:29.820
That's what happened.

00:22:32.390 --> 00:22:33.830
Damn Titans!

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.540 --> 00:23:50.170
Kamille dislikes the relationship between
him and his childhood friend Fa.

00:23:50.380 --> 00:23:53.320
However, as if to strike down
these feelings...

00:23:53.380 --> 00:23:57.550
...Scirocco's Messala prevents
the A.E.U.G. from entering the atmosphere.

00:23:57.790 --> 00:24:02.550
During this battle, Kamille parts with Fa,
and witnesses Kacricon's death.

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:07.560
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Entering the Atmosphere".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Entering The Atmosphere

00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:10.970
You will see the tears of time.
